      <p>Take the following Python code that stores this string: <c>string = "X-DSPAM-Confidence: 0.8475"</c>. Use <c>find</c> and string slicing to extract the portion of the string after the colon character and then use the <c>float</c> function to convert the extracted string into a floating point number called <c>num</c>.</p>
    </statement>
    <program interactive="activecode" language="python" codetailor="all" codetailor-fallback="str-ex-floatq-pp">
      <code>
string = "X-DSPAM-Confidence: 0.8475"

====
